warning[W0004]: directive `{$B+}` is ignored (ignored-directive)
  --> dir_include_warn.inc:1:1
   |
 1 | {$B+}
   | ^^^^^
   |
   = note: boolean operators in Puy always short-circuit
   = note: disable with `{$WARN ignored-directive OFF}`
   = fix: remove `{$B+}`

warning[W0007]: conditional symbol `WIN32` is never defined in Puy (platform-symbol)
  --> dir_include_warn.inc:2:9
   |
 2 | {$IFDEF WIN32}{$ENDIF}
   |         ^^^^^
   |
   = note: a Puy program runs unchanged on every platform, so OS and CPU symbols are never defined
   = note: check the platform at run time with `TOSVersion.Platform`
   = note: disable with `{$WARN platform-symbol OFF}`

